WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.257
This is BizBuddy, shown through the real Next.js application with synthetic shop data.

00:00:05.257 --> 00:00:10.024
Its interface connects daily business reporting, point of sale, and inventory.

00:00:10.024 --> 00:00:14.181
A sale is more than a total: stock and reports must stay consistent.

00:00:14.181 --> 00:00:20.599
The source uses integer money calculations, Supabase authentication, and tenant-scoped PostgreSQL access.

00:00:20.599 --> 00:00:24.266
One hundred and thirty-three selected checks passed locally.

00:00:24.266 --> 00:00:32.090
This capture uses an isolated test database, not a real business account, and does not establish a hosted production deployment.
